/g><g id=\"patch_5\"><path d=\"M 286.474805 139.04 L 376.334545 139.04 L 376.334545 40.04 L 286.474805 40.04 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pd2fb3de91e)\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_6\"><path d=\"M 46.1 139.04 L 46.1 11.528 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_7\"><path d=\"M 46.1 139.04 L 392.06 139.04 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_9\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(99.555325 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\" d=\"M 1920 -77 Q 1414 -77 1068 92 Q 723 262 547 556 Q 371 851 371 1216 Q 371 1670 620 1942 Q 870 2214 1274 2323 L 1274 2374 Q 922 2496 714 2768 Q 506 3040 506 3424 Q 506 3936 880 4240 Q 1254 4544 1920 4544 Q 2586 4544 2960 4240 Q 3334 3936 3334 3424 Q 3334 3040 3126 2768 Q 2918 2496 2566 2374 L 2566 2323 Q 2970 2214 3219 1942 Q 3469 1670 3469 1216 Q 3469 851 3293 556 Q 3117 262 2774 92 Q 2432 -77 1920 -77 z\nM 1920 390 Q 2387 390 2643 601 Q 2899 813 2899 1190 L 2899 1325 Q 2899 1702 2643 1913 Q 2387 2125 1920 2125 Q 1453 2125 1197 1913 Q 941 1702 941 1325 L 941 1190 Q 941 813 1197 601 Q 1453 390 1920 390 z\nM 1920 2573 Q 2336 2573 2557 2755 Q 2778 2938 2778 3277 L 2778 3373 Q 2778 3712 2557 3894 Q 2336 4077 1920 4077 Q 1504 4077 1283 3894 Q 1062 3712 1062 3373 L 1062 3277 Q 1062 2938 1283 2755 Q 1504 2573 1920 2573 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" d=\"M 2912 0 L 2400 0 L 2400 877 L 243 877 L 243 1350 L 2112 4467 L 2912 4467 L 2912 1325 L 3558 1325 L 3558 877 L 2912 877 L 2912 0 z\nM 2368 4051 L 749 1325 L 2400 1325 L 2400 4051 L 2368 4051 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_10\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(211.88 39.16) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_11\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(324.204675 37.84) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pd2fb3de91e\"><rect x=\"46.1\" y=\"11.528\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Value to Redline vs price ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>60% of fees come from rivals and half of them leave: Haulmark loses 30% of its revenue. Standalone value falls to $84M.</p> <p>Total value: $84M + $64M = <b>$148M</b>, below the $150M price. With fewer carriers, the app may also attract fewer shippers, so it could fall further.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> buying Haulmark damages the very thing that makes it valuable: its neutrality.</p>"},{"q":"How else could Redline fill its empty return trips?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Commercial partnership</b> with Haulmark: guaranteed volume on Redline's routes in return for first look at return loads. If it captures 75% of the benefit, that's ~$6M a year, worth about $48M at 8×, for no money up front. Buying is worth about −$2M after the price</li> <li>Use several freight apps at once</li><li>Sign direct contracts with shippers on its main return lanes</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Don't buy Haulmark. On paper it is worth $184M to Redline, but about 60% of its fees come from Redline's rivals, and if half of them leave, the value falls to about $148M, below the $150M price. Instead, agree a partnership that gives Redline first access to return loads on its routes, which captures most of the ~$8M a year benefit without the purchase. Risk: a rival could buy Haulmark, so include a right to bid in the partnership. Next step: approach Haulmark with a volume-for-priority proposal.","great":["Values the deal before and after customer reactions","Spots that neutrality is the asset","Shows the deal flips from positive to negative","Finds a way to get the benefit without buying"],"id":66,"slug":"haulmark"}